(12). A mixture of 9 (220 mg, 0.7 mmol), 2-aminopyrimidine-5-boronic acid
pinacol ester (198 mg, 0.9 mmol, 1.2 equiv), and
bis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(II) chloride (52 mg, 0.07 mmol, 0.1
equiv) in 2 M sodium carbonate solution (0.8 mL) and DMF (3.0 mL) was
charged in a sealed tube, and the mixture was heated at 90 °C for 20 min
under microwave conditions (150 W). The resulting mixture was diluted
with water, and the product was extracted with ethyl acetate. The organic
layer was washed with water and brine, dried over sodium sulfate, and
concentrated. The residue was purified on silica gel (DCM/MeOH), Step 2:
49 was coupled with 2-aminopyrimidine-5-boronic acid pinacol ester under
the same conditions applied to 12 to give
2-[4-(2-amino-pyrimidin-5-yl)-phenyl]-2,3-dimethyl-butyronitrile (98%).
LC/MS (ES+) m/z found 267.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, sealed tube used, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis, SAR, and Series Evolution of Novel Oxadiazole-Containing
5-Lipoxygenase Activating Protein Inhibitors: Discovery of
2-[4-(3-{(R)-1-[4-(2-Amino-pyrimidin-5-yl)-phenyl]-1-cyclopropyl-ethyl}-[1,2,4]oxadiazol-5-yl)-pyrazol-1-yl]-N,N-dimethyl-acetamide
(BI 665915)
